sw: LOK reports mixed script position, line spacing and lists

Superscript, subscript and the line spacing presets read their bool
from the merged item set. An invalid item left the value at zero, so
text half superscript, or paragraphs at 1 and 1.5 lines, read as
off rather than mixed (Ely C08.2). Under LOK an invalid escapement or
line spacing now makes those slots don't-care, as alignment does.

Bullets and numbering said on only when every non-empty paragraph
had them. Under LOK a selection where some paragraphs are listed and
some are not now reports don't-care.
